# ── The loop ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WM_LOOP(B)(L)(X)(J)(fold)(core)(frame)(io) -> run(st): loop until the WM exits
# io = la s. s(display)(infds)(insize)(sim): display(bytes) shows a frame;
# infds lists the input fds; insize is how much to read from one at a time
# ("24" = one event); sim is TRUE for the headless WM, which reads input only
# while no command runs, renders only on request (type-85 records), and stops
# when its input is exhausted and nothing is running.
# Each pass: poll the input fds and every running command's pipe at once, fold
# whatever is ready, and (live) present a new frame if anything changed. The
# recursive call is in tail position, so the VM's TCO keeps the dump bounded.
glyph WM_LOOP = la B. la L. la X. la J. la fold. la core. la frame. la io.
  B(la str_at. la ord. la str_to_int. la int_to_str. la concat. la str_eq.
    la str_len. la add. la sub. la mul. la div. la mod. la lt. la int_eq. la band. la bor.
  L(la nil. la cons. la map. la filter. la find. la append. la nrep. la len.
  X(la poll. la read. la close. la print. la write_file. la exit.
  J(la join. la split.
  core(la empty. la open_win. la handle. la on_output. la job_fds. la shutdown. la welcome.
  io(la display. la infds. la insize. la sim.
  (la C0. la TRUE. la FALSE.
    LET(la st. la n. frame(st)(la bytes. la st2.
